Negative control for the greying law (T2.4 falsifiability, `AC1.4` · `F5` matrix
disposition).

Makes every `never` actor row PICKABLE. The mutation is one line: the matrix
entry test drops its truthiness check and trusts the `"never"` string sentinel
alone. `CLIENT_EMAILS_SCOPE_MATRIX` marks `SELF`/`STAFF`/`GUEST` as
`null as never`, so at runtime those entries are `null` — `String(null)` is the
truthy string `"null"`, and every unsupported actor now resolves a "context
type".

That single change carries the whole defect through the segment, because every
downstream branch keys off `contextType`:

- `actorContexts` reports `contextType: "null"` for the three unsupported
  actors instead of `null`;
- `ActingForSegment`'s `isUnsupported()` goes false, so the row renders as an
  enabled `Button` with no `Tooltip` and no reason;
- the row gains a handler, so it can be chosen — and choosing it arms a context
  type the composable does not resolve, which is exactly the "offer it and fail"
  AC1.4 exists to forbid.

This is a plausible defect, not a strawman: it is the bug of reading a matrix's
sentinel as a string when the matrix spells it `null as never`.

Apply from the repo root: `git apply <this file>`; revert with `git apply -R`.

Reds: the greying cases of
`app/components/scope/__tests__/acting-for-segment.spec.ts` — one row per actor
in the registered matrix, the resolving actor selectable, the `never` actors
`disabled` with the matrix's own reason on a `Tooltip.ce.vue`, and a disabled
row cannot be chosen.

